	So I started up a game, first one in a while, testing the theory
that, having ascended all the hard classes now, many of them with
conducts, I could ascend the easy classes pretty much at will. In
accordance with this, I started up a Val-Hum-Neu-Fem.

	My first attempt was doing nicely to confirm my theory... found
a CoMR in an armor shop on DL2, took a +2 helm off a goblin, found a
chaotic altar (which I quickly converted) on DL3, next door to a general
store, cleared Mine Town (lawful temple in Mine Town, unfortunately),
cleared Sokoban and got a BoH, cleared the main dungeon down to DL13,
past the Big Room, found a saddle and lance and tamed a warhorse, went
back to the Mines to hit Mine's End for the luckstone and to look for a
pickaxe.

	I'd picked up fire resistance from a fire giant and teleport
control from the one tengu that I'd run into, but despite gorging myself
  on everything I could find that could possibly convey poison resistance
  - soldier ants, unicorns (even a gray one that I herded into a corner
for my horse to kill), entire swarms of killer bees - and fixing a lot
of poison damage with my unicorn horn, I hadn't been able to get poison
resistance.

	So of course it was that when returning through the Mines with
two luckstones and pickaxe in hand, with 94 hit points and AC -6, I
tripped over a previously undiscovered dart trap.

